{
  "title": {
    "en": "Competitive Dan Grade Skills Examination"
  },
  "organisation": "British Judo Association",
  "country": "GB",
  "summary": {
    "en": "The BJA's technical examination for promotion to 1st to 5th Dan: single techniques from the British Judo Gokyo, continuation and combination techniques, counters, groundwork chains and escapes, and kata, marked out of ten per technique with pass marks rising by grade."
  },
  "status": "legacy",
  "statusNote": {
    "en": "The examination of the scheme the BJA introduced in 1982, built on 67 techniques, and replaced for promotions from 1 January 2026 by the Competitive Dan Grade Scheme, which examines one set of twenty Kodokan techniques per grade and is transcribed here as a separate examination for each of 1st to 5th Dan. A candidate who had completed this examination by 31 December 2025 keeps it. This page is the record of what was sat until then, and of the syllabus older certificates were awarded against; it is not the form to prepare against for a current grading."
  },
  "source": {
    "title": "Competitive Dan Grade Skills Examination Form (fillable)",
    "date": "January 2020",
    "note": {
      "en": "Transcribed from the official BJA form. The form is the authority; where this page and a current BJA form disagree, the form wins. The Senior Examiner must be at least one grade above the candidate."
    }
  },
  "marking": {
    "en": "Marking ranges from 0 to 10 points for each technique. In the kata sections each technique is demonstrated both right- and left-handed with the combined score recorded, plus a mark out of ten for presentation; a candidate holding a BJA Kata certificate may claim exemption at 65% of the marks. Section requirements are the examiner's choice of one technique from each set in Section 1, and the candidate's choice of sets elsewhere until all sets are required."
  },
